<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">George XI of Kartli</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1651">1651</a>–<a href="/years/1709">1709</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Gurgin Khan, Giorgi XI</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">George XI was king of Kartli in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a>, reigning in 1676-1688 and 1703-1709 under Safavid overlordship. Having accepted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a>, he served the shahs as a commander under the name Gurgin Khan and was made governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kandahar">Kandahar</a> to suppress Afghan unrest. His harsh rule provoked the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghilzai">Ghilzai</a> chief <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mirwais-hotak">Mirwais Hotak</a>, who killed him in 1709 and made Kandahar independent.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/george-xi-of-kartli.jpg" alt="George XI of Kartli" width="320" height="406" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author Derived work: Carnby · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:George_XI_of_Kartli_repaired.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
